<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, this assertion is incorrect because it does not correctly capture the requirement that elements at and after the insertion point should remain the same, except that they are shifted by one position to the right. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

However, the above assert statement does not fully capture the requirement. The correct assertion should ensure that elements before the insertion point remain unchanged, and elements at and after the insertion point are shifted right by one position. Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<\old(this.size()); i<index => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) && i>=index => this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>

This ensures that elements before the insertion point (`i < index`) remain the same, and elements at and after the insertion point (`i >= index`) are shifted right by one position.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
